  "tagline": "Dependency-free SQLite extension for vector search that runs anywhere SQLite does, including WASM.",
  "description": "sqlite-vec is a small C extension by Alex Garcia that adds vector storage and KNN queries to SQLite through vec0 virtual tables and scalar functions, supporting float, int8 and binary vectors with metadata, partition and auxiliary columns. It has no dependencies, so it runs on servers, phones, Raspberry Pis and in the browser via WebAssembly, and it was sponsored by Mozilla Builders. The stable 0.1.x line does brute-force search (fast enough for hundreds of thousands to low millions of vectors); ANN indexes are being developed in the 0.1.10 alphas. Perfect for local-first and on-device RAG.",
